## THE THEOREM

For any conductor whose charge transport is carried by a single channel c, the SG-U1
classification of the circuit under the carrier description is

    Sign_carrier = ( sgn E_c , sgn of c's drift against the conventional arrow ),

while under the conventional description it is (+, +) by construction; and the zero pins
of the formulation - S = 1 inside every hole; Kd_U x T-dagger = 2.6978356e-29 K;
ln rho = 0 today - are INVARIANT under the change of description. The physics does not
depend on which description is used; only the pair transforms, and it transforms by the
carrier's own register sign and drift sign.

COROLLARY (Earth's metal circuits): the carrier is the electron - register E = -5.9297,
occupation pin S-1 = 542.0096 today, drift against the conventional arrow - so the pair
inverts exactly, (+, +) -> (-, -), with every pin unbroken. The sign split between the
drawn circuit and the carried circuit is a freedom of description, resolved by the
register: nature's pair is the carrier's.

